WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

2
00:00:20.658 --> 00:00:22.115
-Hi. Sharon.
-Good morning.

3
00:00:32.549 --> 00:00:33.610
Hi. neighbor.

4
00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:35.347
I'm Sharon Norman.

5
00:00:35.430 --> 00:00:38.190
and as head of the
Neighborhood Welcome Committee.

6
00:00:38.530 --> 00:00:42.010
I welcome you
with this welcome walnut pie.

7
00:00:42.649 --> 00:00:43.649
Wow.

8
00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:45.750
I feel very welcomed.

9
00:00:46.750 --> 00:00:48.470
No sugar. dairy or gluten.

10
00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:49.769
So no flavor.

11
00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:51.730
I'm kidding.

12
00:00:53.275 --> 00:00:55.390
Oh. this is so thoughtful.

13
00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:56.889
I'm Beryl.

14
00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:59.067
Oh. I know all about you.
Beryl Nix.

15
00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:01.467
Uh. or at least
what's public record.

16
00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:03.489
So my reputation precedes me.

17
00:01:03.769 --> 00:01:06.870
We like to know who's joining
our little hamlet here.

18
00:01:07.029 --> 00:01:07.547
"We"?

19
00:01:07.630 --> 00:01:10.390
We are a very close-knit
community.

20
00:01:10.750 --> 00:01:13.787
and you lucked out living
next door to me.

21
00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:16.387
I am the head
of the Garden Club.

22
00:01:16.470 --> 00:01:17.930
the PTA. the Social Committee.

23
00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:19.127
Social Committee?

24
00:01:19.210 --> 00:01:21.169
So you know where
I can get the good drugs.

25
00:01:22.389 --> 00:01:23.750
Kidding again. Sharon.

26
00:01:24.009 --> 00:01:27.206
Oh. I could tell
you were gonna be fun.

27
00:01:27.289 --> 00:01:28.750
Guilty as charged.

28
00:01:29.030 --> 00:01:31.387
But I moved here
to get away from all the fun

29
00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:33.590
of the city and its...
everything.

30
00:01:34.209 --> 00:01:38.009
The quiet nothing of here
will help me focus on my art.

31
00:01:38.350 --> 00:01:40.230
You'll find there's
a lot of life here.

32
00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:43.250
This is our community calendar.

33
00:01:43.489 --> 00:01:46.667
And while we do not have an HOA.
I put together a list

34
00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:49.750
of suggested guidelines
that we like to follow.

35
00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:52.149
Oh. can't wait
to meet this "we."

36
00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:55.070
It's things like
outdoor light wattages.

37
00:01:55.189 --> 00:01:58.507
noise considerations
like the wind chimes

38
00:01:58.590 --> 00:02:02.106
that you put in
over the weekend on your yard.

39
00:02:02.189 --> 00:02:06.110
They haven't broken any
noise ordinances... yet.

40
00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:10.009
-Just kidding.
-You got me.

41
00:02:13.860 --> 00:02:15.370
Oh. landscape maintenance.

42
00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:19.610
You know. that big old wild tree
on our property line

43
00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:22.250
blocks a lot of
the natural light to my studio.

44
00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:26.730
Again. these are just
suggested guidelines.

45
00:02:27.310 --> 00:02:29.126
This is our Towering Maple.

46
00:02:29.209 --> 00:02:32.327
and it has been sort of
grandfathered in.

47
00:02:32.410 --> 00:02:33.410
Is it?

48
00:02:34.969 --> 00:02:36.916
We find that very convenient.

49
00:02:37.907 --> 00:02:42.462
Anyway. thank you for the pie.
rules and hopefully drugs.

50
00:02:43.155 --> 00:02:44.707
Just kidding. neighbor.

51
00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.160
Do we have new blossoms?

52
00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.100
Ugh. I am buying her shades.

53
00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:24.960
Phil will open up his shop
early for me.

54
00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:26.500
It's not a big deal.

55
00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:28.817
I was looking at the painting.
It's not bad.

56
00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:30.080
The '60s are dead. honey.

57
00:03:30.380 --> 00:03:31.660
She's not even a real artist.

58
00:03:31.780 --> 00:03:33.317
She's just rich and bored.

59
00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.000
And cold. apparently.

60
00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:37.700
I see more nudity
at work every day.

61
00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.880
The sordid life
of an anesthesiologist.

62
00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:41.240
Indeed.

63
00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:42.800
Have a good day. please.

64
00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:43.960
I always do.

65
00:03:59.140 --> 00:04:01.339
Beryl is having a party again.

66
00:04:01.500 --> 00:04:02.839
We're invited. Could be fun.

67
00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.060
Ugh.

68
00:04:04.419 --> 00:04:05.336
Hard pass.

69
00:04:05.419 --> 00:04:07.459
And she's again asking us
to trim the tree.

70
00:04:07.639 --> 00:04:09.659
"The Towering is overpowering."

71
00:04:09.939 --> 00:04:11.936
Rad. Doughnuts.

72
00:04:12.019 --> 00:04:14.119
Absolutely not.
No. this is bribery.

73
00:04:14.217 --> 00:04:16.329
Put that back.

74
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:21.279
Take an apple. Go upstairs.
This is adult stuff.

75
00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:23.819
Seems pretty childish to me.

76
00:04:34.800 --> 00:04:36.280
The only thing worse
than wind chimes:

77
00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:38.760
drum circles.

78
00:04:39.699 --> 00:04:41.439
She's keeping me awake
on purpose.

79
00:04:42.079 --> 00:04:43.359
Well. at least
she's on the beat.

80
00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.300
Come back to bed.

81
00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:49.520
It's so funny to you.

82
00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:52.197
You're gone all day.
and I'm dealing with

83
00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:54.340
this tension and harassment.

84
00:04:54.620 --> 00:04:56.199
Honey. I'm in an operating room.

85
00:04:58.300 --> 00:05:01.016
And how many years
have I come home to you

86
00:05:01.099 --> 00:05:02.937
fired up about noise

87
00:05:03.020 --> 00:05:05.076
or too many cars parked
on the street or the...

88
00:05:05.159 --> 00:05:06.440
the arbor rights fight?

89
00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:09.000
The maple is a bit unruly.

90
00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:11.759
Do you remember
when we found this house?

91
00:05:13.439 --> 00:05:15.139
We walked up that drive.

92
00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:18.000
we saw that tree.

93
00:05:19.460 --> 00:05:20.760
and we both knew

94
00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:24.260
that we were gonna make
this house our home.

95
00:05:24.700 --> 00:05:27.780
And under that unruly maple...

96
00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:32.257
...we'd lie there
and you'd read to me

97
00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:33.840
with my belly out to here.

98
00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:36.260
That's where Avery took
her first steps.

99
00:05:36.439 --> 00:05:38.040
That's where she tested
her bravery

100
00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:41.699
and she climbed higher and
higher under our watchful gaze.

101
00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:45.360
And when I see our...

102
00:05:46.680 --> 00:05:49.400
Towering Maple on the horizon.

103
00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:53.580
I know that I am almost home.

104
00:05:55.819 --> 00:05:59.740
It grows. and it grows with us.

105
00:06:03.399 --> 00:06:06.000
I didn't realize how important
that tree is to you.

106
00:06:06.919 --> 00:06:07.919
It's family.

107
00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:13.650
And no member
of our family will ever.

108
00:06:14.130 --> 00:06:16.730
ever be touched by that woman.

109
00:06:17.589 --> 00:06:18.787
Your tree is dead.

110
00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:20.910
But how? What happened?

111
00:06:21.110 --> 00:06:22.110
It's nature. man.

112
00:06:22.930 --> 00:06:24.550
It sucks sometimes.

113
00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:26.247
Oh. Sharon.

114
00:06:26.330 --> 00:06:27.330
I'm so sorry.

115
00:06:28.610 --> 00:06:31.470
It was such a massive presence
in all our lives.

116
00:06:40.430 --> 00:06:43.247
And the final Halloween event
on the agenda is

117
00:06:43.330 --> 00:06:44.607
the Haunted Maze.

118
00:06:44.690 --> 00:06:47.430
And this year.
it goes to Beryl Nix.

119
00:06:49.090 --> 00:06:52.427
I will email you the names
of the high school volunteers

120
00:06:52.510 --> 00:06:53.947
who are going to help. and...

121
00:06:54.030 --> 00:06:55.350
Well. Sharon.
we've been talking.

122
00:06:55.950 --> 00:06:56.607
"We"?

123
00:06:56.690 --> 00:06:57.807
The ladies and I

124
00:06:57.890 --> 00:07:00.550
think this year
I should amp up the maze.

125
00:07:01.070 --> 00:07:03.010
Make it really. really scary.

126
00:07:03.449 --> 00:07:06.250
unlike past... no offense...
boring years.

127
00:07:06.590 --> 00:07:07.590
No offense.

128
00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:08.850
None taken.

129
00:07:10.190 --> 00:07:12.630
But we don't want
to traumatize the kids.

130
00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:14.167
Brayden had to sleep in bed

131
00:07:14.250 --> 00:07:16.046
with you for a week
after last year's.

132
00:07:16.129 --> 00:07:18.090
That's because he saw
a real spider in the maze.

133
00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:21.347
I think Beryl has a great idea...
spice it up.

134
00:07:21.430 --> 00:07:22.470
Okay.

135
00:07:23.130 --> 00:07:24.407
What did you have in mind?

136
00:07:24.490 --> 00:07:25.327
Oh. you know me.

137
00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:28.410
I take inspiration here.
there. everywhere. so...

138
00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:31.370
I haven't settled
on my vision just yet.

139
00:07:31.629 --> 00:07:36.367
but I do see me in the center
in a fabulous display.

140
00:07:36.450 --> 00:07:37.527
Where are you going to get

141
00:07:37.610 --> 00:07:40.050
your costumes. props.
lighting. fog machines?

142
00:07:40.190 --> 00:07:41.690
You know. there isn't much time.

143
00:07:42.350 --> 00:07:43.390
My brain.

144
00:07:43.670 --> 00:07:46.290
I don't have the space to think
of all the nuts and bolts.

145
00:07:46.610 --> 00:07:48.887
To realize the horror and gore

146
00:07:48.970 --> 00:07:51.470
deserving of our community.
I'll need help.

147
00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:53.170
-Ah. Ah!
-Anyone?

148
00:07:53.266 --> 00:07:54.773
I'd love to.

149
00:07:54.870 --> 00:07:56.910
-You? You. too?
-Yeah.

150
00:07:57.090 --> 00:07:59.090
-Oh. every... Oh. great.
-Yeah.

151
00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:00.350
Fine. I'll help.

152
00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:04.807
I'm very busy.
but I live next door.

153
00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:08.090
and my event is locked in.

154
00:08:08.389 --> 00:08:10.029
Well. you're the best
of the best.

155
00:08:10.430 --> 00:08:11.430
Thank you. Sharon.

156
00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:13.110
You're welcome.

157
00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:14.647
Great.

158
00:08:14.730 --> 00:08:16.069
I'm gonna be so excited.

159
00:08:16.470 --> 00:08:17.387
Do you know what I'm thinking.

160
00:08:17.470 --> 00:08:18.990
is some found objects.

161
00:08:19.099 --> 00:08:20.637
-Yeah.
-And material.

162
00:08:20.747 --> 00:08:22.395
like. from the neighborhood.

163
00:08:33.309 --> 00:08:34.309
Congratulations.

164
00:08:34.409 --> 00:08:35.929
You're halfway there.

165
00:08:36.370 --> 00:08:37.849
Collect your candy.

166
00:08:39.097 --> 00:08:41.669
The maze is closing
for the costume contest.

167
00:08:42.090 --> 00:08:44.970
Hurry. or the Headless Horseman
will catch you.

168
00:08:58.322 --> 00:08:59.661
Boo!

169
00:08:59.799 --> 00:09:00.799
Mom.

170
00:09:01.299 --> 00:09:02.600
You do this every year.

171
00:09:02.799 --> 00:09:05.019
Because Jump-Scare-Crow works
every year.

172
00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:06.680
-Mm-hmm.
-Hey. where's your costume?

173
00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:08.120
Um...

174
00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:12.900
See? Are you happy?

175
00:09:13.289 --> 00:09:14.313
Purr-fectly.

176
00:09:14.396 --> 00:09:16.644
-Mm-hmm.
-Okay. Go have fun. Be safe.

177
00:09:40.027 --> 00:09:41.204
Sharon?

178
00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:53.139
Good morning.

179
00:09:54.920 --> 00:09:56.920
Hi. Can I help you?

180
00:09:57.420 --> 00:09:58.420
I'm good.

181
00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:00.020
Classic Beryl.

182
00:10:00.240 --> 00:10:02.717
After a wild night.
she usually isn't awake

183
00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:04.740
or home until later.

184
00:10:05.600 --> 00:10:08.159
Uh. well. we're just here
to clean up the maze props.

185
00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:09.540
We've got a schedule.

186
00:10:10.120 --> 00:10:11.460
Oh. Go ahead.

187
00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:13.037
I hereby grant you permission

188
00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:15.080
as president of the
Neighborhood Events Committee.

189
00:10:15.820 --> 00:10:17.659
A signature would do better.

190
00:10:18.320 --> 00:10:19.320
You got it.

191
00:10:21.040 --> 00:10:22.040
Happy Halloween.

192
00:10:33.799 --> 00:10:34.959
Why do we have an extra head?

193
00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:41.200
Oh. my God.

194
00:10:41.760 --> 00:10:42.760
You're a genius.

195
00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:44.980
Not my design. but I'll take it.

196
00:10:45.759 --> 00:10:47.720
Hey. Rivers. check this out.

197
00:10:48.160 --> 00:10:49.277
If you hold down the space bar.

198
00:10:49.360 --> 00:10:51.040
you can move your cursor
wherever you want.

199
00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:52.420
How did I not know that?

200
00:10:52.560 --> 00:10:54.057
You know.
I'll be impressed with IT

201
00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:56.280
when you guys upgrade our Wi-Fi.

202
00:10:56.560 --> 00:10:57.477
IT?

203
00:10:57.560 --> 00:10:58.997
Desk duty wouldn't be
half as bad

204
00:10:59.080 --> 00:11:01.340
if our Internet wasn't
Stone Age dial-up.

205
00:11:01.480 --> 00:11:04.200
Well. you know. in IT. we say
that patience is a virtue.

206
00:11:04.680 --> 00:11:05.597
It builds character.

207
00:11:05.680 --> 00:11:08.820
Something someone on desk duty
may need.

208
00:11:08.924 --> 00:11:10.792
ELSBETH [Cockney accent]:
Out of my way. love.

209
00:11:10.896 --> 00:11:12.661
Out of my way.

210
00:11:12.800 --> 00:11:14.140
I love it.

211
00:11:14.340 --> 00:11:15.360
Hey. Julia.

212
00:11:16.220 --> 00:11:17.560
To what do we owe the honor?

213
00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:18.717
You know. just here

214
00:11:18.800 --> 00:11:20.140
-helping the old man.
-Hi. hon.

215
00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:22.660
-Right on time.
-Hi. Daddy. And you're not.

216
00:11:22.879 --> 00:11:24.879
Head into my office.
I'll be in there in a second.

217
00:11:25.020 --> 00:11:26.020
Oh.

218
00:11:26.180 --> 00:11:27.960
ELSBETH [Cockney accent]:
Not without these.

219
00:11:28.460 --> 00:11:29.780
Thank you. Eliza.

220
00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:31.720
We got a call.

221
00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:33.120
It's a case outside the city.

222
00:11:33.220 --> 00:11:34.220
They found a...

223
00:11:35.540 --> 00:11:37.577
Halloween is over.
What's going on?

224
00:11:37.660 --> 00:11:41.195
Cap'n. 'alloween ain't
just one day.

225
00:11:41.340 --> 00:11:42.360
In here. it is.

226
00:11:43.040 --> 00:11:43.957
Okay. the truth is

227
00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:45.320
my costumes arrived late.

228
00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:48.397
But how do you pick just one
My Fair Ladycostume?

229
00:11:48.480 --> 00:11:51.900
You can't.
so I'm doing Halloweek.

230
00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:53.440
I thought you were from Newsies.

231
00:11:53.740 --> 00:11:55.100
Either way.
you're gonna love this.

232
00:11:55.460 --> 00:11:56.699
They found a severed head.

233
00:11:57.760 --> 00:11:59.941
Oh!

234
00:12:00.220 --> 00:12:01.220
Whoa. cool.

235
00:12:01.680 --> 00:12:03.040
But you're never gonna
guess where.

236
00:12:03.540 --> 00:12:04.540
Great Neck?

237
00:12:07.799 --> 00:12:10.359
I thought we picked up
all of our props.

238
00:12:10.639 --> 00:12:12.636
We just kind of scoop
and then sort 'em later

239
00:12:12.719 --> 00:12:14.698
-at our warehouse in the city.
-Mm.

240
00:12:14.781 --> 00:12:16.016
Well. with the owner dead.

241
00:12:16.099 --> 00:12:17.697
who let you in
to do all the scooping?

242
00:12:17.780 --> 00:12:18.919
-Who's in charge here?
-Ugh.

243
00:12:20.419 --> 00:12:21.419
Her.

244
00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:23.537
Now. if you'll excuse me.

245
00:12:23.620 --> 00:12:25.640
these nice suburban ladies
freak me out.

246
00:12:25.939 --> 00:12:28.576
Where is Sheriff Pete?
Why is the NYPD here?

247
00:12:28.659 --> 00:12:29.919
We are all terrified.

248
00:12:30.319 --> 00:12:32.559
Well. I'm Detective Donnelly.
and this is Elsa?

249
00:12:32.674 --> 00:12:34.039
SHARON and ELSBETH: Eliza.

250
00:12:34.122 --> 00:12:35.199
Thank you.

251
00:12:35.380 --> 00:12:37.060
But really. Elsbeth Tascioni.

252
00:12:37.839 --> 00:12:38.756
And you are?

253
00:12:38.839 --> 00:12:40.540
Sharon Norman. I live next door.

254
00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:42.856
and I am president of the
Neighborhood Safety Committee.

255
00:12:42.939 --> 00:12:44.779
so I demand to know.
what is going on here?

256
00:12:44.940 --> 00:12:46.620
Well. we found a body
in Manhattan.

257
00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:48.819
which is why we're. uh.
covering the case.

258
00:12:48.940 --> 00:12:51.199
And that body appears
to have come from this maze.

259
00:12:51.859 --> 00:12:52.859
Beryl Nix.

260
00:12:54.486 --> 00:12:55.559
Not Beryl.

261
00:12:56.259 --> 00:12:59.379
I knew that she should not
have hired those outsiders.

262
00:12:59.679 --> 00:13:00.799
Who are those men?

263
00:13:00.959 --> 00:13:02.459
Uh. well. he goes by Chop.

264
00:13:03.419 --> 00:13:04.419
Enough said.

265
00:13:04.539 --> 00:13:06.279
He said it's because
he likes chopped salad.

266
00:13:06.959 --> 00:13:08.939
Do you know how Beryl died?

267
00:13:09.079 --> 00:13:10.817
Because you didn't even ask

268
00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:12.480
before going straight
to blaming Chop.

269
00:13:12.819 --> 00:13:14.519
Well. it is simple math.

270
00:13:14.799 --> 00:13:16.639
Somebody died
with people like that around?

271
00:13:16.919 --> 00:13:20.459
I was not raised to be nosy.
but I-I have to know...

272
00:13:21.379 --> 00:13:22.379
what happened?

273
00:13:22.919 --> 00:13:25.379
We found her head.
then her body.

274
00:13:25.579 --> 00:13:26.974
-Oh...
-How long have you been neighbors?

275
00:13:27.057 --> 00:13:29.506
Heavens. Uh...

276
00:13:29.719 --> 00:13:32.159
Let's see. It's. uh...
it's hard to think.

277
00:13:34.114 --> 00:13:35.559
Uh...

278
00:13:35.649 --> 00:13:37.470
She moved in. um...

279
00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:41.629
...May 3. 2022.

280
00:13:42.909 --> 00:13:44.730
Were you friends?

281
00:13:44.970 --> 00:13:45.970
You close or...

282
00:13:46.310 --> 00:13:49.270
No. but we were neighborly.

283
00:13:49.590 --> 00:13:52.030
And let's just say she had
a different lifestyle.

284
00:13:52.510 --> 00:13:54.470
but I respected her

285
00:13:54.870 --> 00:13:56.669
and she respected...

286
00:13:58.750 --> 00:13:59.830
I'm so sorry.

287
00:14:00.190 --> 00:14:01.607
I'm just on edge. and...

288
00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:03.650
this is very. very scary.

289
00:14:04.150 --> 00:14:05.267
I have to alert the neighborhood

290
00:14:05.350 --> 00:14:06.750
that there is
a killer on the loose.

291
00:14:07.870 --> 00:14:08.870
Can you believe it?

292
00:14:10.234 --> 00:14:12.996
Someone beheaded
in Sleepy Hollow?

293
00:14:16.821 --> 00:14:19.883
Abso-bloomin'-lutely.

294
00:14:29.200 --> 00:14:32.497
All right. Dad. so. once again.
we're going up here and...

295
00:14:32.580 --> 00:14:33.617
I-I-I got it.

296
00:14:33.700 --> 00:14:34.700
Okay. Let's see.

297
00:14:37.203 --> 00:14:38.423
What the...

298
00:14:39.329 --> 00:14:41.626
-I did everything right.
-Because you went to print.

299
00:14:41.709 --> 00:14:43.390
but you have to choose
"Save as PDF."

300
00:14:43.689 --> 00:14:45.049
Well. how does that make
any sense?

301
00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:49.000
Come in.

302
00:14:49.180 --> 00:14:51.377
Captain. I have an update
on the. um...

303
00:14:51.460 --> 00:14:54.037
I'm sorry. I can come back if...

304
00:14:54.120 --> 00:14:56.100
No. Uh. I welcome
the interruption.

305
00:14:56.299 --> 00:14:58.316
This is my daughter. Julia.
Julia. Cameron.

306
00:14:58.399 --> 00:14:59.399
He's one of our MEs.

307
00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:00.700
-Hi.
-Hi.

308
00:15:01.039 --> 00:15:02.039
Uh. you were saying?

309
00:15:02.299 --> 00:15:03.757
Yes. So. um. we established

310
00:15:03.840 --> 00:15:07.037
Beryl Nix's exact time of death
from her wrist fitness tracker's

311
00:15:07.120 --> 00:15:08.017
heart rate monitor.

312
00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:09.700
Exact? Uh. that's helpful.

313
00:15:09.960 --> 00:15:11.956
The PPG tech
with optical heart rate sensors

314
00:15:12.039 --> 00:15:13.980
used in fitness trackers
is pretty accurate.

315
00:15:14.139 --> 00:15:15.619
Certainly makes my job
a lot easier.

316
00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:17.437
Do you have one?

317
00:15:17.520 --> 00:15:19.197
No. I'm a software engineer

318
00:15:19.280 --> 00:15:21.260
who avoids exercise
if at all possible.

319
00:15:22.359 --> 00:15:23.147
She's here to help

320
00:15:23.230 --> 00:15:24.600
her old man with. uh.

321
00:15:24.880 --> 00:15:26.080
some tech issues.

322
00:15:26.460 --> 00:15:28.080
I'm the most patient
of all his kids.

323
00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:30.557
I don't like the way
the IT guys here talk to me.

324
00:15:30.640 --> 00:15:31.657
like I don't know
what I'm doing.

325
00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:32.740
No. I-I get it. Um...

326
00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:35.300
I've been trying to update
my department's software.

327
00:15:35.520 --> 00:15:36.820
but. I mean. I'm afraid to ask.

328
00:15:37.039 --> 00:15:38.740
And I don't even know
where to start.

329
00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:39.917
I can help.

330
00:15:40.000 --> 00:15:41.400
If you're looking
for a better CMS.

331
00:15:41.640 --> 00:15:43.020
there's some good COTS options.

332
00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:46.340
Right.

333
00:15:47.938 --> 00:15:49.230
How about this? Uh...

334
00:15:49.353 --> 00:15:50.368
Let's grab lunch today.

335
00:15:50.460 --> 00:15:51.659
Uh. we're having lunch.

336
00:15:52.159 --> 00:15:53.077
Right.

337
00:15:53.160 --> 00:15:54.857
Well. how about coffee
before work

338
00:15:54.940 --> 00:15:56.740
-day after tomorrow?
-Great. Yes.

339
00:15:56.960 --> 00:15:58.920
I will brush up
on my acronyms before then.

340
00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:01.620
Here's my number.

341
00:16:01.799 --> 00:16:02.860
Just text me.

342
00:16:02.967 --> 00:16:04.411
Here you go.

343
00:16:04.519 --> 00:16:06.279
Will do. Thanks. Julia.

344
00:16:06.620 --> 00:16:07.620
Mm-hmm.

345
00:16:07.720 --> 00:16:08.720
Captain.

346
00:16:11.500 --> 00:16:12.500
What?

347
00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:15.040
Come on. Back to it.
Captain Luddite.

348
00:16:15.920 --> 00:16:16.837
Come on.

349
00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:19.400
Thank you so much
for letting me talk to you.

350
00:16:19.820 --> 00:16:22.517
Everyone says
you're "the person who'd know"

351
00:16:22.600 --> 00:16:23.920
when it comes
to the neighborhood.

352
00:16:24.340 --> 00:16:26.559
I do like to stay connected.

353
00:16:26.664 --> 00:16:29.110
Your yard is...

354
00:16:29.216 --> 00:16:30.917
oh so loverly.

355
00:16:31.059 --> 00:16:33.456
Thank you. I have won
Green Thumb of the Year

356
00:16:33.539 --> 00:16:34.537
six years running.

357
00:16:34.620 --> 00:16:35.477
Congratulations.

358
00:16:35.560 --> 00:16:37.520
My grandmother
had a green thumb.

359
00:16:37.820 --> 00:16:38.820
She adored violets.

360
00:16:39.059 --> 00:16:41.620
I'm more of a "sell-uh"
than a "grow-uh."

361
00:16:41.820 --> 00:16:43.337
Well. it relaxes me. Which is...

362
00:16:43.420 --> 00:16:45.217
...what I need
at a time like this.

363
00:16:45.300 --> 00:16:47.659
Have those maze roustabouts
been arrested yet?

364
00:16:48.179 --> 00:16:49.179
"Roustabouts"?

365
00:16:49.419 --> 00:16:51.200
You are really convinced
it was them.

366
00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:54.840
Well. all I know is that.
one day. our community is safe

367
00:16:54.940 --> 00:16:56.740
and. the next day.
there is a loose head.

368
00:16:56.860 --> 00:16:59.340
And the only thing
that changed was them.

369
00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:00.860
So. the sooner you arrest them.

370
00:17:00.960 --> 00:17:02.720
the sooner
we will be safe again.

371
00:17:03.539 --> 00:17:06.880
Well. Chop and his crew were
on break when Beryl died.

372
00:17:07.079 --> 00:17:08.057
Getting high. no doubt.

373
00:17:08.140 --> 00:17:09.240
On cheese.

374
00:17:10.020 --> 00:17:12.319
They were sharing the cutest

375
00:17:13.040 --> 00:17:15.417
little Halloween-themed
charcuterie board

376
00:17:15.500 --> 00:17:17.276
on their truck.
One of the workers

377
00:17:17.359 --> 00:17:19.079
is in culinary school.

378
00:17:19.400 --> 00:17:20.920
It had these little olive...

379
00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:23.040
eyeballs.

380
00:17:23.180 --> 00:17:24.097
Little teeth.

381
00:17:24.180 --> 00:17:25.180
Anyway.

382
00:17:26.839 --> 00:17:28.380
we are looking local now.

383
00:17:28.740 --> 00:17:29.860
Where were you on Halloween?

384
00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:36.019
Wow. those wind chimes
carry. huh?

385
00:17:36.640 --> 00:17:37.640
I don't even notice.

386
00:17:39.079 --> 00:17:40.859
Um. if you need to know.

387
00:17:41.000 --> 00:17:44.900
on Halloween. I was doing
my customary Jump-Scare-Crow.

388
00:17:46.099 --> 00:17:47.560
Which everybody loves.

389
00:17:47.799 --> 00:17:49.339
I. uh. sit on my front porch.

390
00:17:49.440 --> 00:17:51.579
and then when kids come
to trick-or-treat. I jump!

391
00:17:53.118 --> 00:17:54.119
And scare them.

392
00:17:55.372 --> 00:17:57.070
See? I got you.

393
00:17:57.153 --> 00:17:58.797
So you can ask any of the kids

394
00:17:58.880 --> 00:18:00.920
who were brave enough
to visit my porch.

395
00:18:01.339 --> 00:18:02.339
Oh. Right.

396
00:18:02.479 --> 00:18:04.200
Uh. speaking of your porch.

397
00:18:04.780 --> 00:18:06.180
I noticed the plaque.

398
00:18:07.000 --> 00:18:08.400
"Towering Maple."

399
00:18:09.319 --> 00:18:10.319
Was that the maple?

400
00:18:10.579 --> 00:18:11.819
Your home's namesake?

401
00:18:13.850 --> 00:18:16.550
You must have been devastated
to lose that.

402
00:18:17.969 --> 00:18:18.969
It's nature.

403
00:18:19.569 --> 00:18:20.810
It sucks sometimes.

404
00:18:23.350 --> 00:18:26.527
You know.
things just come and go

405
00:18:26.610 --> 00:18:28.870
and live and die. but...

406
00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:32.326
...our house will
remain Towering Maple

407
00:18:32.409 --> 00:18:33.770
with or without that tree.

408
00:18:34.569 --> 00:18:35.589
Well. that's sweet.

409
00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:37.590
Speaking of coming and going...

410
00:18:38.989 --> 00:18:41.949
...as I said.
I am not one to be nosy.

411
00:18:42.090 --> 00:18:45.270
but have the police talked
to any of the many men

412
00:18:45.965 --> 00:18:47.537
that would visit Beryl

413
00:18:47.620 --> 00:18:48.989
at all hours of the night?

414
00:18:49.072 --> 00:18:52.946
Some marriages may last longer
now that she's gone.

415
00:18:53.029 --> 00:18:55.689
Well. we'll definitely look
into that.

416
00:18:56.429 --> 00:18:58.908
'Cause I am nosy.

417
00:19:02.285 --> 00:19:03.485
Oh.

418
00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:05.940
Lots of neighborhood husbands.

419
00:19:06.260 --> 00:19:07.260
according to Sharon.

420
00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:08.639
Yeah. lots of suspects.

421
00:19:08.780 --> 00:19:09.780
according to me.

422
00:19:10.100 --> 00:19:11.300
You know. Sharon knows

423
00:19:11.679 --> 00:19:13.000
everything about her neighbors.

424
00:19:13.099 --> 00:19:15.259
And. meanwhile.
I haven't even met one of mine.

425
00:19:16.859 --> 00:19:18.259
How does that work?

426
00:19:18.620 --> 00:19:20.257
Well. that's the beauty
of New York.

427
00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:21.620
is everyone minds
their business.

428
00:19:22.159 --> 00:19:24.180
You're only separated
by a wall or floor.

429
00:19:24.580 --> 00:19:26.460
In these small towns
and suburbs.

430
00:19:26.659 --> 00:19:28.357
you get more space
but less privacy.

431
00:19:28.440 --> 00:19:29.478
Mm.

432
00:19:29.561 --> 00:19:30.759
I suppose.

433
00:19:31.159 --> 00:19:35.540
But I'd like to know who I'm
sharing walls and floors with.

434
00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:37.737
I accidentally dropped one

435
00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:39.620
of Gonzo's favorite toys
in the hall.

436
00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:43.020
I put up notices.
and no one reached out.

437
00:19:43.340 --> 00:19:45.877
Well. just because you don't
know your neighbors doesn't mean

438
00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:47.276
that they're not looking out
for you.

439
00:19:47.359 --> 00:19:48.359
You'll see.

440
00:19:49.000 --> 00:19:51.099
That's very optimistic of you.

441
00:19:51.519 --> 00:19:52.799
Must be all the Halloween candy.

442
00:19:54.799 --> 00:19:56.000
No costume today?

443
00:19:57.659 --> 00:19:58.659
Never mind.

444
00:19:59.159 --> 00:20:00.159
Do we have any leads?

445
00:20:00.399 --> 00:20:01.399
Maybe too many.

446
00:20:01.839 --> 00:20:03.579
Whittle them down
and keep me posted.

447
00:20:03.685 --> 00:20:05.707
Oh. uh. Cap'n?

448
00:20:05.849 --> 00:20:07.161
Cap'n.

449
00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:13.279
I've been trying not to ask.
but any update on Kaya?

450
00:20:13.660 --> 00:20:14.660
Oh. No.

451
00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:16.440
But I'm sure she's fine.

452
00:20:16.900 --> 00:20:18.180
She's probably on her next case.

453
00:20:18.540 --> 00:20:20.140
This is the life
of undercover work.

454
00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:21.500
I understand.

455
00:20:21.680 --> 00:20:23.160
I just... I miss my friend.

456
00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:25.300
And I'm worried about her.

457
00:20:25.900 --> 00:20:27.800
Well. I know one thing.

458
00:20:29.279 --> 00:20:30.859
Kaya would love your costume.

459
00:20:32.660 --> 00:20:33.660
What costume?

460
00:20:34.279 --> 00:20:35.279
Who's that?

461
00:20:41.150 --> 00:20:42.827
I should've known better
than to trust you.

462
00:20:42.910 --> 00:20:44.370
Psycho.
I thought you were chill.

463
00:20:44.470 --> 00:20:46.167
I am chill. Until I'm not.

464
00:20:46.250 --> 00:20:47.350
And now I'm not.

465
00:20:47.650 --> 00:20:49.190
Don't come back! Ever!

466
00:20:49.287 --> 00:20:50.431
I won't!

467
00:20:50.530 --> 00:20:51.930
Me and Ave would
hang at Beryl's.

468
00:20:52.290 --> 00:20:55.170
We could eat. watch.
smoke what we wanted.

469
00:20:55.430 --> 00:20:56.710
Our parents are uptight as hell.

470
00:20:57.370 --> 00:20:58.870
-"Ave"?
-Avery.

471
00:20:59.410 --> 00:21:01.470
-Avery Norman.
-Sharon Norman's daughter?

472
00:21:01.810 --> 00:21:02.810
Queen Uptight herself.

473
00:21:03.350 --> 00:21:05.170
Are you supposed
to be Cruella de Vil?

474
00:21:05.470 --> 00:21:07.047
-Oh. Come on.
-We have

475
00:21:07.130 --> 00:21:09.177
footage of you running
from Beryl's

476
00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:11.810
and her chasing after you
and yelling.

477
00:21:11.930 --> 00:21:15.079
You're the only person
that left Beryl's unhappy.

478
00:21:15.170 --> 00:21:16.087
Lovers' quarrel?

479
00:21:16.170 --> 00:21:17.170
Dude. No.

480
00:21:17.590 --> 00:21:19.170
She caught me taking
her pain pills.

481
00:21:19.630 --> 00:21:21.347
She had so many.
I didn't think she'd notice.

482
00:21:21.430 --> 00:21:23.110
But she did.
and you saw what happened.

483
00:21:23.370 --> 00:21:24.730
We certainly did. Xander.

484
00:21:25.430 --> 00:21:26.430
What do you mean?

485
00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:28.450
Detective Donnelly

486
00:21:29.150 --> 00:21:31.970
is under the assumption that...

487
00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:34.927
whomever stole

488
00:21:35.010 --> 00:21:39.590
their pain pills did make them
meet their demise.

489
00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:41.147
What?

490
00:21:41.230 --> 00:21:44.390
I didn't make anybody
meet their demise.

491
00:21:44.890 --> 00:21:45.890
What is that accent?

492
00:21:46.070 --> 00:21:47.470
If anybody. it was Ave.

493
00:21:47.570 --> 00:21:48.630
She wanted to kill her.

494
00:21:48.850 --> 00:21:50.510
-Why don't I believe you?
-I swear.

495
00:21:50.670 --> 00:21:51.670
Look at these texts.

496
00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:58.340
"Oh. God. if that bitch
calls the cops on you.

497
00:21:58.439 --> 00:21:59.356
I'll kill her."

498
00:21:59.439 --> 00:22:02.579
Garn...

499
00:22:07.262 --> 00:22:09.093
"Save as"?

500
00:22:09.200 --> 00:22:10.620
You wanted to see me?

501
00:22:10.779 --> 00:22:11.779
Yes.

502
00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:13.140
Close the door.

503
00:22:19.500 --> 00:22:21.720
I know you can't tell me much.
but...

504
00:22:22.459 --> 00:22:23.459
how's Kaya?

505
00:22:24.359 --> 00:22:26.559
Correct. Um. I can't.

506
00:22:26.820 --> 00:22:28.280
But as far as I know.

507
00:22:28.540 --> 00:22:29.640
she's fine.

508
00:22:29.920 --> 00:22:31.800
And I'm sure
she'd appreciate you asking.

509
00:22:32.460 --> 00:22:33.519
Well. that's good to hear.

510
00:22:34.680 --> 00:22:38.499
Out of sight
but not out of mind. right?

511
00:22:39.548 --> 00:22:42.940
Because some other people
are in sight.

512
00:22:43.859 --> 00:22:44.940
You know what I mean?

513
00:22:46.160 --> 00:22:47.160
Sir?

514
00:22:47.540 --> 00:22:49.140
There are two people
that I care about

515
00:22:49.500 --> 00:22:50.900
that I don't want to see hurt...

516
00:22:52.960 --> 00:22:53.877
Kaya...

517
00:22:53.960 --> 00:22:54.960
...and Julia.

518
00:22:55.960 --> 00:22:58.078
Sir. no. our coffee...

519
00:22:58.839 --> 00:23:00.200
...it's purely professional.

520
00:23:00.319 --> 00:23:01.319
I know my daughter.

521
00:23:01.619 --> 00:23:04.217
That may not be true
on both ends. so...

522
00:23:04.300 --> 00:23:07.020
why don't we simplify things

523
00:23:07.679 --> 00:23:08.900
for everyone involved?

524
00:23:10.180 --> 00:23:11.380
I understand. sir.

525
00:23:12.240 --> 00:23:14.039
Sorry for any misunderstanding.

526
00:23:14.147 --> 00:23:15.310
Mm.

527
00:23:16.220 --> 00:23:17.220
Not at all.

528
00:23:26.450 --> 00:23:27.450
We all got

529
00:23:27.570 --> 00:23:29.347
Ring cameras because you said.

530
00:23:29.430 --> 00:23:30.727
"More eyes. less crimes."

531
00:23:30.810 --> 00:23:33.290
-And look how that worked out.
-And you found the maze crew.

532
00:23:33.490 --> 00:23:37.330
-The call is coming from inside the house. Sharon.
-That's very interesting.

533
00:23:37.423 --> 00:23:39.106
-Sharon.
-I mean. am I wrong? Now she has nothing to say.

534
00:23:39.189 --> 00:23:41.265
-Now she has nothing to say.
-Quiet!

535
00:23:42.630 --> 00:23:43.950
How dare you?

536
00:23:45.370 --> 00:23:49.110
I have dedicated my life
to this neighborhood.

537
00:23:51.070 --> 00:23:52.430
And it was safe.

538
00:23:53.550 --> 00:23:54.550
Until now.

539
00:23:54.930 --> 00:23:56.250
So what changed?

540
00:23:57.050 --> 00:23:58.770
Hmm? Exactly.

541
00:23:59.410 --> 00:24:04.550
I think we have all learned
a very valuable lesson.

542
00:24:05.509 --> 00:24:07.130
Have the police made an arrest?

543
00:24:07.510 --> 00:24:08.590
I can't say.

544
00:24:08.690 --> 00:24:10.287
But I'm in close communication
with them.

545
00:24:10.370 --> 00:24:11.470
and it should be soon.

546
00:24:14.530 --> 00:24:17.009
Do pardon our intrusion.

547
00:24:17.590 --> 00:24:18.347
Ladies.

548
00:24:18.430 --> 00:24:20.150
We need to talk to Sharon alone.

549
00:24:20.790 --> 00:24:22.667
Well. we're
in the middle of a meeting. so...

550
00:24:22.750 --> 00:24:24.670
We're gonna need to talk
to you about some texts.

551
00:24:24.890 --> 00:24:25.890
And Avery.

552
00:24:26.470 --> 00:24:27.470
Avery?

553
00:24:28.690 --> 00:24:29.607
Avery?

554
00:24:29.690 --> 00:24:31.790
I swear I was not at Beryl's
on Halloween.

555
00:24:32.310 --> 00:24:34.830
-But you did write those texts?
-Well. yeah.

556
00:24:35.010 --> 00:24:36.410
But I didn't mean anything.

557
00:24:36.910 --> 00:24:39.007
You went to Beryl's? When?

558
00:24:39.090 --> 00:24:42.970
Avery. where were you
on Halloween at 8:47 p.m.?

559
00:24:44.110 --> 00:24:45.110
It's okay.

560
00:24:45.730 --> 00:24:47.567
You can tell them.
You were volunteering

561
00:24:47.650 --> 00:24:48.710
at the costume contest.

562
00:24:49.090 --> 00:24:50.130
But I wasn't.

563
00:24:50.610 --> 00:24:52.670
Avery. were you
with that Xander boy?

564
00:24:52.830 --> 00:24:54.467
-I am gonna make you go upstairs right now.
-No. Oh. my God.

565
00:24:54.550 --> 00:24:55.610
I was with Dad.

566
00:24:56.009 --> 00:24:57.070
I hate costumes.

567
00:24:57.450 --> 00:24:58.556
I don't even like Halloween.

568
00:24:58.639 --> 00:25:00.170
I haven't liked it
since I was 12.

569
00:25:00.450 --> 00:25:01.207
That must have been

570
00:25:01.290 --> 00:25:04.410
so tough for a girl growing up
in Sleepy Hollow.

571
00:25:04.910 --> 00:25:06.590
Again. where were you?

572
00:25:07.990 --> 00:25:10.070
My dad and I go out to eat
on Halloween.

573
00:25:10.670 --> 00:25:11.587
Excuse me.

574
00:25:11.670 --> 00:25:13.950
Your father was supposedly
working late.

575
00:25:14.950 --> 00:25:15.990
Do you have proof of this?

576
00:25:22.950 --> 00:25:25.110
You were at Splitz's Diner?

577
00:25:26.130 --> 00:25:28.750
-By the mall?
-You never let me do anything fun.

578
00:25:28.890 --> 00:25:32.250
Why is the photo album
titled "MFT"?

579
00:25:34.710 --> 00:25:37.549
Go ahead. It's not like
it could get any worse.

580
00:25:38.250 --> 00:25:39.250
Um...

581
00:25:39.490 --> 00:25:40.570
"Mom-Free Time."

582
00:25:40.670 --> 00:25:43.009
It's stuff my dad and I
do together without Mom.

583
00:25:44.470 --> 00:25:45.470
Sorry. Mom.

584
00:25:45.810 --> 00:25:47.227
Well. the metadata on the photo

585
00:25:47.310 --> 00:25:50.087
shows it was taken around
the same time that Beryl died.

586
00:25:50.170 --> 00:25:51.170
But...

587
00:25:51.430 --> 00:25:54.446
it is possible that. uh.
Avery could have been involved.

588
00:25:54.529 --> 00:25:56.130
-with a few minutes to spare.
-Mm.

589
00:25:57.690 --> 00:25:58.990
No. it's not possible.

590
00:26:01.500 --> 00:26:03.160
She doesn't know the maze.

591
00:26:03.440 --> 00:26:04.460
It would take too long.

592
00:26:05.140 --> 00:26:07.100
Well. there's only one way
to find out.

593
00:26:07.229 --> 00:26:09.083
Take me through it.

594
00:26:10.059 --> 00:26:11.500
I'm gonna stay here with Avery.

595
00:26:13.650 --> 00:26:15.227
I am great

596
00:26:15.310 --> 00:26:18.127
at puzzles. and do you see
how long this is taking me?

597
00:26:18.210 --> 00:26:20.047
There is no way
that my daughter did this.

598
00:26:20.130 --> 00:26:21.890
I knew that Xander boy
was trouble.

599
00:26:22.009 --> 00:26:23.470
He only got into state schools.

600
00:26:23.730 --> 00:26:24.887
Oh. we actually cleared him.

601
00:26:24.970 --> 00:26:27.367
Yeah. he has a shoulder injury
from lacrosse.

602
00:26:27.450 --> 00:26:29.167
so he couldn't have lifted
the murder weapon.

603
00:26:29.250 --> 00:26:30.647
And that would be?

604
00:26:30.730 --> 00:26:31.487
Oh. Right.

605
00:26:31.570 --> 00:26:32.969
Um. it was a chain saw.

606
00:26:34.050 --> 00:26:37.390
Yeah. We found it
in Beryl's art studio.

607
00:26:37.509 --> 00:26:40.799
-Oh. my God.
-So. Xander started stealing Beryl's pain pills

608
00:26:41.190 --> 00:26:43.747
for his shoulder pain when his
doctor wouldn't prescribe more.

609
00:26:43.830 --> 00:26:45.447
Unbelievable.
It just goes to show.

610
00:26:45.530 --> 00:26:48.110
you have no idea what's going on
in your neighbor's house.

611
00:26:48.330 --> 00:26:49.630
Yeah. Or your own.

612
00:26:50.210 --> 00:26:52.247
I saw the look of pain
on your face

613
00:26:52.330 --> 00:26:54.467
when you learned
about Mom-Free Time.

614
00:26:54.550 --> 00:26:56.900
You think you're in control.

615
00:26:57.410 --> 00:26:59.207
You think you know things.

616
00:26:59.290 --> 00:27:01.567
But most things are outside
of anyone's control.

617
00:27:01.650 --> 00:27:02.890
Especially as a parent.

618
00:27:02.990 --> 00:27:03.990
Don't you agree?

619
00:27:04.130 --> 00:27:05.130
Not at all.

620
00:27:05.340 --> 00:27:07.617
That is a lazy excuse
for not being involved.

621
00:27:07.700 --> 00:27:09.899
I have dedicated my life to...

622
00:27:10.140 --> 00:27:11.220
Being involved?

623
00:27:12.740 --> 00:27:13.537
Caring.

624
00:27:13.620 --> 00:27:16.800
Now. is it left or is it right?

625
00:27:17.100 --> 00:27:18.920
Hmm. Oh. wait.

626
00:27:19.040 --> 00:27:19.957
So. hold on. Hold on.

627
00:27:20.040 --> 00:27:22.495
The call is pausing the timer.

628
00:27:22.578 --> 00:27:25.389
Salutations.

629
00:27:26.604 --> 00:27:27.521
They're gonna charge her?

630
00:27:27.604 --> 00:27:29.180
But she's a minor.

631
00:27:29.760 --> 00:27:30.760
Avery?

632
00:27:30.940 --> 00:27:33.080
They're cuffing her now?
On camera?

633
00:27:38.299 --> 00:27:39.216
Wow!

634
00:27:39.299 --> 00:27:41.740
You move bloody fast!

635
00:27:41.919 --> 00:27:43.919
Avery?! Wh-Where is she?

636
00:27:44.180 --> 00:27:45.180
Is she under arrest?

637
00:27:45.899 --> 00:27:46.899
Avery?

638
00:27:48.139 --> 00:27:49.639
Oh. You mean the call?

639
00:27:49.780 --> 00:27:50.697
Oh. no. no. no. no.

640
00:27:50.780 --> 00:27:52.537
Detective Donnelly and I
were catching up

641
00:27:52.620 --> 00:27:54.080
on my favorite reality show

642
00:27:54.460 --> 00:27:55.460
Lavish Ladies.

643
00:27:55.620 --> 00:27:57.300
Oh. the drama never ends.

644
00:27:57.639 --> 00:27:59.220
No. Avery's fine.

645
00:27:59.619 --> 00:28:00.619
Oh. thank God.

646
00:28:01.139 --> 00:28:02.139
Oh.

647
00:28:02.659 --> 00:28:05.777
Oh. thank God. Let me just catch
my breath and we'll...

648
00:28:05.860 --> 00:28:06.637
resume the maze.

649
00:28:06.720 --> 00:28:08.480
Uh. no. Not necessary.

650
00:28:09.280 --> 00:28:10.280
I got what I needed.

651
00:28:10.520 --> 00:28:13.100
You navigated your way
in and out of that maze.

652
00:28:13.840 --> 00:28:14.880
no problem.

653
00:28:15.539 --> 00:28:16.799
So this was a test?

654
00:28:17.480 --> 00:28:19.340
-Of course.
-Of what?

655
00:28:19.560 --> 00:28:21.139
My mama bear adrenaline?

656
00:28:21.579 --> 00:28:22.720
Is that all?

657
00:28:23.159 --> 00:28:25.819
You helped Beryl
organize that maze.

658
00:28:25.919 --> 00:28:28.379
No doubt.
you had a copy of the plans.

659
00:28:28.819 --> 00:28:31.479
You know every square inch
of that maze.

660
00:28:32.279 --> 00:28:35.799
You big-city cops
are unbelievable.

661
00:28:36.179 --> 00:28:37.519
I'm not a cop.

662
00:28:37.720 --> 00:28:38.799
I'm a lady.

663
00:28:39.360 --> 00:28:40.919
You come to our town

664
00:28:41.080 --> 00:28:44.060
and you accuse one
of our innocent high school boys

665
00:28:44.200 --> 00:28:47.320
and then you accuse
my innocent daughter

666
00:28:47.580 --> 00:28:48.642
and then you accuse...

667
00:28:48.725 --> 00:28:49.933
me.

668
00:28:50.066 --> 00:28:53.086
The one person
that cares the most

669
00:28:53.220 --> 00:28:55.679
about the safety
of this neighborhood.

670
00:28:55.839 --> 00:28:58.776
Well. you know. why not?

671
00:28:58.859 --> 00:29:01.240
Let's just throw it on Sharon.

672
00:29:01.679 --> 00:29:04.179
Because everybody blames
everything on me anyway.

673
00:29:04.980 --> 00:29:06.654
That's what I get for...

674
00:29:08.091 --> 00:29:09.380
...for trying to help.

675
00:29:09.639 --> 00:29:10.880
That's not true.

676
00:29:11.159 --> 00:29:13.040
A lot of good
can come from helping.

677
00:29:13.899 --> 00:29:15.019
So. help.

678
00:29:15.700 --> 00:29:17.777
Show us big-city cops
how wrong we are

679
00:29:17.860 --> 00:29:19.020
so we can focus elsewhere.

680
00:29:20.440 --> 00:29:22.100
How can I help you if...

681
00:29:22.779 --> 00:29:24.060
you don't believe me?

682
00:29:25.800 --> 00:29:26.477
Well.

683
00:29:26.560 --> 00:29:30.240
you said you were
on your porch all night.

684
00:29:30.679 --> 00:29:31.596
Right?

685
00:29:31.679 --> 00:29:34.040
So don't tell us...

686
00:29:34.300 --> 00:29:35.300
show us.

687
00:29:35.600 --> 00:29:37.076
It's in your control

688
00:29:37.159 --> 00:29:38.960
to prove your innocence.

689
00:29:40.000 --> 00:29:40.816
There's...

690
00:29:40.899 --> 00:29:42.380
a Ring camera

691
00:29:43.459 --> 00:29:45.020
at your house. isn't there?

692
00:29:49.100 --> 00:29:50.100
Yeah.

693
00:29:51.899 --> 00:29:53.399
Whatever's so funny?

694
00:29:54.139 --> 00:29:55.056
Nothing.

695
00:29:55.139 --> 00:29:57.199
I will get you that footage.

696
00:29:57.480 --> 00:30:00.300
And you will see
that I was there.

697
00:30:01.399 --> 00:30:02.399
All night.

698
00:30:10.400 --> 00:30:14.097
We saw you on Sharon Norman's
Ring camera footage

699
00:30:14.180 --> 00:30:16.219
looking very comfortable
with a chain saw.

700
00:30:16.920 --> 00:30:18.560
Well. yeah. I hope so.

701
00:30:18.660 --> 00:30:19.920
I cut down trees for a living.

702
00:30:20.320 --> 00:30:23.519
Was one of those trees
Sharon's Towering Maple?

703
00:30:24.640 --> 00:30:25.557
Yeah.

704
00:30:25.640 --> 00:30:26.880
Why did you cut that down?

705
00:30:27.680 --> 00:30:28.680
It was dead.

706
00:30:29.400 --> 00:30:30.700
How did it die?

707
00:30:30.980 --> 00:30:32.957
Old age? I don't know.

708
00:30:33.040 --> 00:30:35.460
How did Sharon feel about it?

709
00:30:35.840 --> 00:30:36.840
Feel? Fine.

710
00:30:37.020 --> 00:30:38.427
Listen. I don't get into stuff
like that.

711
00:30:38.510 --> 00:30:39.197
It's bad for business.

712
00:30:39.280 --> 00:30:41.140
So. if you spend your days

713
00:30:41.320 --> 00:30:42.557
sawing through big trees.

714
00:30:42.640 --> 00:30:44.257
it wouldn't take you long at all

715
00:30:44.340 --> 00:30:47.420
to saw through something
a little bit easier like...

716
00:30:48.060 --> 00:30:49.060
Whoa.

717
00:30:49.160 --> 00:30:50.160
What?

718
00:30:51.080 --> 00:30:53.040
Did a lady really get her head
cut off?

719
00:30:53.400 --> 00:30:54.840
And why are you dressed
like that?

720
00:30:55.100 --> 00:30:57.900
-Is this a prank show?
-It can feel like that sometimes.

721
00:30:58.120 --> 00:31:00.037
Why did you say
it was bad for business?

722
00:31:00.120 --> 00:31:02.920
Look. I like dealing
with earth stuff. not people.

723
00:31:03.140 --> 00:31:04.537
I don't want to get called in
for lawsuits.

724
00:31:04.620 --> 00:31:06.640
I cut. I dispose.
and I don't ask questions.

725
00:31:06.980 --> 00:31:08.497
What kind of questions
would there be?

726
00:31:08.580 --> 00:31:11.317
A lot of trees
that suddenly die of "old age"

727
00:31:11.400 --> 00:31:12.920
are on property lines.

728
00:31:20.400 --> 00:31:22.280
Sorry to tell you this.

729
00:31:22.440 --> 00:31:25.680
but your Towering Maple
may have been poisoned.

730
00:31:28.340 --> 00:31:29.340
Poisoned?

731
00:31:29.458 --> 00:31:31.057
Mm. No. Unlikely.

732
00:31:31.140 --> 00:31:32.260
Weren't you ever suspicious?

733
00:31:32.759 --> 00:31:35.200
It died so suddenly.
according to your tree doctor.

734
00:31:35.860 --> 00:31:39.360
If Beryl poisoned the tree. then
I'm sure it was an accident.

735
00:31:39.780 --> 00:31:41.176
Why are we talking about this?

736
00:31:41.259 --> 00:31:43.137
Didn't my Ring cam footage
show that I was here?

737
00:31:43.220 --> 00:31:45.440
I never said Beryl did it.

738
00:31:45.560 --> 00:31:47.720
Well. who else
could it possibly have been?

739
00:31:47.840 --> 00:31:49.277
She used chemicals in her art.

740
00:31:49.360 --> 00:31:53.420
If the tree was poisoned. then
let's just say it was Beryl.

741
00:31:53.660 --> 00:31:54.660
Okay. let's.

742
00:31:55.740 --> 00:31:57.180
Then I forgive her.

743
00:31:57.760 --> 00:31:59.820
Because there are
more important things in life.

744
00:32:00.200 --> 00:32:01.597
I'm just surprised.

745
00:32:01.680 --> 00:32:05.920
Because if someone poisoned
the namesake of my home. I'd...

746
00:32:06.350 --> 00:32:08.840
You'd have to learn
to let things go. Eliza.

747
00:32:09.560 --> 00:32:10.560
Like you said.

748
00:32:11.200 --> 00:32:13.680
not everything
is in your control.

749
00:32:14.420 --> 00:32:15.817
Now. if you don't mind?

750
00:32:15.900 --> 00:32:17.200
Oh. [posh accent]: Of course.

751
00:32:18.580 --> 00:32:21.000
I have a ball to get to anyway.

752
00:32:27.000 --> 00:32:28.560
I just hope...

753
00:32:29.760 --> 00:32:33.140
...the poison doesn't affect
the rest of your beautiful yard.

754
00:32:34.500 --> 00:32:36.320
I appreciate your concern.

755
00:32:36.820 --> 00:32:38.180
but I'm not worried.

756
00:32:38.819 --> 00:32:41.440
What I am worried about is.
there's a killer on the loose.

757
00:32:42.160 --> 00:32:43.160
Me. too.

758
00:32:43.260 --> 00:32:45.100
But it shouldn't be much longer.

759
00:32:51.049 --> 00:32:53.129
You warned Cameron off me.
didn't you?

760
00:32:54.510 --> 00:32:55.510
Go on.

761
00:32:55.610 --> 00:32:57.610
What are you worried about?
You're the boss. right?

762
00:32:59.350 --> 00:33:00.450
Cameron has work to do.

763
00:33:01.210 --> 00:33:03.046
How it affects his social life
is up to him.

764
00:33:03.129 --> 00:33:04.450
I knew you would do this.

765
00:33:04.690 --> 00:33:06.787
You never miss the chance
to throw your power around

766
00:33:06.870 --> 00:33:08.470
-to mess with my life.
-Oh. is that so?

767
00:33:08.953 --> 00:33:09.898
-Yes.
-It's your life.

768
00:33:09.981 --> 00:33:11.249
But this precinct
and these people.

769
00:33:11.332 --> 00:33:12.972
it's my world.

770
00:33:13.069 --> 00:33:14.809
That is so classic.

771
00:33:15.389 --> 00:33:17.627
You know I'm the only one
of your kids you'd do this to.

772
00:33:17.710 --> 00:33:18.947
-Oh. come on.
-Be real. Dad.

773
00:33:19.030 --> 00:33:20.427
If one of them came in here

774
00:33:20.510 --> 00:33:22.250
and hit it off
with one of your officers.

775
00:33:22.370 --> 00:33:24.470
you'd pull that officer in
and warn them off?

776
00:33:24.850 --> 00:33:25.767
Huh?

777
00:33:25.850 --> 00:33:27.369
Look at me
and tell me that's true.

778
00:33:28.290 --> 00:33:29.290
I only...

779
00:33:30.389 --> 00:33:31.649
ever want to protect you.

780
00:33:32.049 --> 00:33:33.049
I'm 27.

781
00:33:33.730 --> 00:33:35.849
I'm not this kid
you keep framed in your desk.

782
00:33:35.950 --> 00:33:37.169
I don't need your protection.

783
00:33:37.630 --> 00:33:39.190
I may one day want
your approval.

784
00:33:39.510 --> 00:33:41.409
But only when I ask for it.

785
00:33:41.930 --> 00:33:42.847
Got it.

786
00:33:42.930 --> 00:33:43.930
You're 27.

787
00:33:44.210 --> 00:33:45.210
You know everything.

788
00:33:45.490 --> 00:33:46.490
Well. hotshot.

789
00:33:47.250 --> 00:33:50.047
why don't you tell me why
I saved this file to my desktop

790
00:33:50.130 --> 00:33:51.470
and it's not there. huh?

791
00:33:52.030 --> 00:33:53.030
I can't with you.

792
00:33:54.309 --> 00:33:55.309
Julia.

793
00:34:03.500 --> 00:34:04.500
Damn it.

794
00:34:05.480 --> 00:34:07.680
Any updates on Gonzo's toy?

795
00:34:08.060 --> 00:34:09.340
Oh. No.

796
00:34:09.639 --> 00:34:10.639
Not yet.

797
00:34:11.000 --> 00:34:13.056
This whole case has me thinking

798
00:34:13.139 --> 00:34:14.699
maybe I don't want
to know my neighbors.

799
00:34:15.040 --> 00:34:17.179
Eh. Don't get cynical
like the rest of us.

800
00:34:17.380 --> 00:34:18.380
Not yet.

801
00:34:19.239 --> 00:34:20.239
So far.

802
00:34:20.360 --> 00:34:21.800
Sharon's alibi checks out.

803
00:34:22.079 --> 00:34:24.340
It's not helpful that
she's off-screen. but still.

804
00:34:24.480 --> 00:34:25.598
Mm.

805
00:34:25.739 --> 00:34:27.579
Isn't that convenient?

806
00:34:28.820 --> 00:34:31.460
Ugh. I just know she did it.

807
00:34:32.120 --> 00:34:35.277
I watched her dig up her plants

808
00:34:35.360 --> 00:34:38.679
and replace the soil
the day after the murder.

809
00:34:39.340 --> 00:34:41.257
My grandma used to let me
help her in the garden.

810
00:34:41.340 --> 00:34:45.039
There's no reason to do all that
unless she knew

811
00:34:45.518 --> 00:34:48.559
the poison from the tree
would spread.

812
00:34:49.059 --> 00:34:50.440
But how did she kill Beryl?

813
00:34:51.780 --> 00:34:53.139
There's the time of death.

814
00:34:53.360 --> 00:34:55.880
and we haven't seen Sharon move.

815
00:34:56.699 --> 00:34:58.960
-So it seems.
-One. two.

816
00:34:59.340 --> 00:35:00.659
three. four.

817
00:35:01.000 --> 00:35:03.020
-five.
-Just you wait.

818
00:35:03.440 --> 00:35:04.659
Sharon Norman.

819
00:35:05.219 --> 00:35:06.639
Just you wait.

820
00:35:22.297 --> 00:35:25.661
♪ I ♪

821
00:35:26.761 --> 00:35:28.718
♪ I... ♪

822
00:35:28.821 --> 00:35:30.023
Do you mind?!

823
00:35:30.126 --> 00:35:31.396
Oh.

824
00:35:31.499 --> 00:35:34.267
I thought you didn't notice
Beryl's wind chimes.

825
00:35:34.350 --> 00:35:36.438
This is starting to feel
like harassment.

826
00:35:36.739 --> 00:35:38.507
And it was cute at first.

827
00:35:38.590 --> 00:35:39.836
with the costumes. but...

828
00:35:39.919 --> 00:35:41.879
you're doing a lot.

829
00:35:42.219 --> 00:35:43.600
Even for Sleepy Hollow.

830
00:35:43.960 --> 00:35:44.877
Halloween is over.

831
00:35:44.960 --> 00:35:47.639
Oh. It's not over just yet.

832
00:35:47.879 --> 00:35:50.279
We have one more scare.

833
00:35:51.379 --> 00:35:52.439
We solved the murder!

834
00:35:53.819 --> 00:35:54.736
How?

835
00:35:54.819 --> 00:35:55.859
A fingerprint.

836
00:35:56.439 --> 00:35:57.779
Come on. I'll show you.

837
00:35:58.699 --> 00:35:59.699
In there?

838
00:36:01.949 --> 00:36:04.406
I never got a chance
to go through the maze

839
00:36:04.489 --> 00:36:05.710
when it was all dressed up.

840
00:36:05.819 --> 00:36:06.943
So...

841
00:36:08.827 --> 00:36:11.799
God.

842
00:36:11.910 --> 00:36:14.470
No. this chain saw is
from Chop's crew.

843
00:36:15.350 --> 00:36:16.350
Doesn't have a chain.

844
00:36:16.569 --> 00:36:17.569
See?

845
00:36:17.929 --> 00:36:20.449
None of their chain saws
had chains.

846
00:36:20.809 --> 00:36:23.247
You assumed
that those outsider roustabouts

847
00:36:23.330 --> 00:36:24.450
didn't care about safety.

848
00:36:24.750 --> 00:36:26.030
But that was their top priority.

849
00:36:26.409 --> 00:36:28.346
So I'll give them
a good Yelp review.

850
00:36:28.429 --> 00:36:29.066
What do I care?

851
00:36:29.149 --> 00:36:31.710
You thought.
with all of their chain saws.

852
00:36:32.210 --> 00:36:33.870
they'd be blamed
for Beryl's death.

853
00:36:34.210 --> 00:36:35.489
Don't be ridiculous.

854
00:36:35.929 --> 00:36:38.689
Why would I care
who is blamed for Beryl's death?

855
00:36:38.929 --> 00:36:39.929
Why. indeed.

856
00:36:40.429 --> 00:36:41.429
Shall we?

857
00:36:44.250 --> 00:36:47.750
Oh. Would you stop?

858
00:36:48.470 --> 00:36:49.470
This...

859
00:36:49.730 --> 00:36:50.850
is the murder weapon.

860
00:36:51.126 --> 00:36:52.885
Beryl's chain saw.

861
00:36:53.570 --> 00:36:55.350
You used this

862
00:36:55.890 --> 00:36:57.070
to kill her

863
00:36:57.190 --> 00:36:59.910
and then you stashed it back
in her art studio.

864
00:37:01.037 --> 00:37:02.309
And then you gave Chop's crew
permission

865
00:37:02.392 --> 00:37:03.572
to clean up the crime scene.

866
00:37:03.690 --> 00:37:05.769
Your frame job complete.

867
00:37:06.050 --> 00:37:09.630
you assumed your role
of concerned neighbor.

868
00:37:10.130 --> 00:37:12.827
I am a concerned neighbor.

869
00:37:12.910 --> 00:37:14.090
You hated Beryl.

870
00:37:14.530 --> 00:37:16.927
Everyone knew it.
Your own daughter had to hide

871
00:37:17.010 --> 00:37:18.290
that she spent time with her.

872
00:37:18.510 --> 00:37:20.550
Hating your neighbor
does not make you a murderer.

873
00:37:20.989 --> 00:37:22.769
Beryl was a nuisance
to this neighborhood.

874
00:37:23.010 --> 00:37:24.927
Ask around. Everyone will agree.

875
00:37:25.010 --> 00:37:26.226
We could not stand her.

876
00:37:26.309 --> 00:37:27.949
Now. where is
this damn fingerprint?

877
00:37:29.150 --> 00:37:30.289
I did ask around.

878
00:37:32.650 --> 00:37:34.170
What are you all doing here?

879
00:37:34.950 --> 00:37:36.170
-Hi. Sharon.
-Hi. Sharon.

880
00:37:37.430 --> 00:37:38.347
Oh. honey.

881
00:37:38.430 --> 00:37:39.690
-Avery.
-Mom.

882
00:37:40.310 --> 00:37:41.310
Beryl was cool.

883
00:37:41.530 --> 00:37:42.769
She let me be myself.

884
00:37:43.150 --> 00:37:44.190
And we loved her.

885
00:37:44.410 --> 00:37:46.329
She had us trying fun new things
all the time.

886
00:37:46.470 --> 00:37:48.030
What are you talking about?

887
00:37:48.210 --> 00:37:50.070
She was sleeping
with all of your husbands.

888
00:37:50.410 --> 00:37:52.010
She wasn't sleeping with them.

889
00:37:52.309 --> 00:37:54.206
She was teaching them pottery
to surprise us.

890
00:37:54.289 --> 00:37:55.927
We've all gotten ashtrays

891
00:37:56.010 --> 00:37:57.630
-for our birthdays.
-And anniversary.

892
00:37:58.370 --> 00:37:59.370
He could've done better.

893
00:37:59.670 --> 00:38:00.967
We should have known when you

894
00:38:01.050 --> 00:38:04.270
wanted to help Beryl with
something actually fun for once.

895
00:38:04.550 --> 00:38:05.550
For once?

896
00:38:05.889 --> 00:38:07.070
I don't deserve this.

897
00:38:08.630 --> 00:38:10.250
Show me the evidence now.

898
00:38:10.750 --> 00:38:11.790
We did find a fingerprint.

899
00:38:12.450 --> 00:38:14.110
But it wasn't on the chain saw.

900
00:38:14.210 --> 00:38:16.250
And it wasn't
the murderer's fingerprint.

901
00:38:18.389 --> 00:38:19.306
Okay.

902
00:38:19.389 --> 00:38:20.650
That's Tommy Forst.

903
00:38:20.830 --> 00:38:22.827
-Keep watching.
-And brave little Tommy

904
00:38:22.910 --> 00:38:26.170
was dared by his friends
to hold your hand.

905
00:38:26.321 --> 00:38:28.176
-One. two...
-But the time stamp shows

906
00:38:28.328 --> 00:38:30.972
-it was the exact moment that Beryl was murdered.
-...three. four.

907
00:38:31.055 --> 00:38:32.411
-five.
-And you didn't move.

908
00:38:32.494 --> 00:38:34.430
I don't scare everyone.

909
00:38:34.730 --> 00:38:35.726
Tommy is a sensitive boy.

910
00:38:35.809 --> 00:38:37.670
I did not want
to traumatize him.

911
00:38:37.770 --> 00:38:39.427
We found
your Jump-Scare-Crow dummy

912
00:38:39.510 --> 00:38:40.850
in the back of your garage.

913
00:38:41.289 --> 00:38:43.789
And on its rubber glove...
Tommy's fingerprints.

914
00:38:44.430 --> 00:38:47.350
Proving that you weren't on the
porch at the time of the murder.

915
00:38:48.650 --> 00:38:51.950
I probably went to the bathroom
and changed out the dummy.

916
00:38:52.690 --> 00:38:55.170
That's a perfectly reasonable
explanation.

917
00:38:55.690 --> 00:38:59.250
But the fingerprint was
just enough to get us a warrant.

918
00:38:59.769 --> 00:39:02.726
We tested the pipes
of the washing machine

919
00:39:02.809 --> 00:39:06.470
where you washed the scrubs that
you wore when you killed Beryl.

920
00:39:06.630 --> 00:39:08.510
And. well...

921
00:39:09.350 --> 00:39:11.890
we found a little bit of Beryl.

922
00:39:15.290 --> 00:39:17.210
Why didn't you just say that
from the beginning?!

923
00:39:17.510 --> 00:39:18.750
I hate mazes!

924
00:39:19.610 --> 00:39:20.327
Because...

925
00:39:20.410 --> 00:39:23.090
it's the perfect end
to Halloweek.

926
00:39:23.710 --> 00:39:25.809
And it really brought
the neighborhood together.

927
00:39:26.350 --> 00:39:28.450
How could you all love Beryl?!

928
00:39:28.870 --> 00:39:30.050
She was a killer!

929
00:39:30.610 --> 00:39:32.410
She was my tree killer!

930
00:39:32.930 --> 00:39:34.110
Actually. honey. that was me.

931
00:39:34.890 --> 00:39:35.527
I-I thought

932
00:39:35.610 --> 00:39:38.847
that removing the tree would end
your petty feud with Beryl.

933
00:39:38.930 --> 00:39:40.647
But no matter
how perfect our life was.

934
00:39:40.730 --> 00:39:41.890
you could never be happy.

935
00:39:43.309 --> 00:39:44.869
You're all gonna miss me.

936
00:39:45.750 --> 00:39:47.689
-You're gonna regret this.
-Oh...

937
00:39:47.850 --> 00:39:50.867
I think Sleepy Hollow
will be just fine

938
00:39:50.950 --> 00:39:52.970
without Sharon Norman.

939
00:39:53.118 --> 00:39:55.088
Ha.

940
00:39:55.199 --> 00:39:57.139
That was my last one. I promise.

941
00:39:57.460 --> 00:39:58.480
I'll write up the report.

942
00:39:59.039 --> 00:40:00.039
How's this?

943
00:40:00.660 --> 00:40:02.960
"Trace amounts of blood
of the slain

944
00:40:03.379 --> 00:40:05.619
stayed mainly in the drain."

945
00:40:07.179 --> 00:40:10.619
-Needs work.
-Oh. no. it's perfect.

946
00:40:15.000 --> 00:40:16.440
You deleted your cloud?

947
00:40:17.880 --> 00:40:18.477
No.

948
00:40:18.560 --> 00:40:20.100
I don't even know what that is.

949
00:40:21.360 --> 00:40:22.640
But I knew
it would get you here.

950
00:40:23.659 --> 00:40:24.659
Good ploy.

951
00:40:30.800 --> 00:40:32.039
I'm sorry. kid.

952
00:40:32.820 --> 00:40:34.560
I know it's a cliché.
but it's true.

953
00:40:35.060 --> 00:40:36.797
It's hard...

954
00:40:36.880 --> 00:40:39.640
...for parents to accept
their kids as adults.

955
00:40:41.460 --> 00:40:43.620
Well. me at least.

956
00:40:46.150 --> 00:40:49.750
Every day
I looked at this photo...

957
00:40:51.390 --> 00:40:52.390
...on my desk...

958
00:40:53.990 --> 00:40:55.570
...of my little girl.

959
00:40:57.889 --> 00:41:00.267
At the girl I was raising
to be independent

960
00:41:00.350 --> 00:41:02.390
and to make her own choices...

961
00:41:02.570 --> 00:41:04.190
Don't take all the credit.

962
00:41:04.849 --> 00:41:06.050
Mom did most of it.

963
00:41:06.212 --> 00:41:08.936
Hey now.

964
00:41:09.100 --> 00:41:10.680
But here in front of me...

965
00:41:12.399 --> 00:41:13.399
...is that adult.

966
00:41:15.860 --> 00:41:18.760
Inserting myself
as if I know best

967
00:41:19.260 --> 00:41:20.960
was me being a bad dad.

968
00:41:27.349 --> 00:41:30.029
I'll know better moving forward.

969
00:41:32.250 --> 00:41:34.230
How did you get
this picture printed?

970
00:41:34.690 --> 00:41:37.590
Uh. it wasn't easy.
let me tell you.

971
00:41:41.300 --> 00:41:43.077
You could never be a bad dad.

972
00:41:43.160 --> 00:41:44.980
Oh.

973
00:41:48.419 --> 00:41:49.417
Oh. That's for me.

974
00:41:49.500 --> 00:41:50.500
I have a dinner date.

975
00:41:51.580 --> 00:41:53.379
Don't worry. It's not Cameron.

976
00:41:57.520 --> 00:41:58.437
-Hey.
-Good night. Daddy.

977
00:41:58.520 --> 00:42:00.120
Good night. Dad... er. um...

978
00:42:01.120 --> 00:42:02.120
Captain.

979
00:42:02.441 --> 00:42:04.452
-Sir. Uh. you know. I'm...
-Mm. Mm-hmm. mm-hmm.

980
00:42:04.579 --> 00:42:05.579
Love you.

981
00:42:07.259 --> 00:42:08.259
Oh.

982
00:42:09.900 --> 00:42:10.900
Damn.

983
00:42:12.740 --> 00:42:15.040
Damn. damn. damn.

984
00:42:27.561 --> 00:42:28.913
Thank you!

985
00:42:29.853 --> 00:42:31.617
Whoever you are.

986
00:42:32.351 --> 00:42:33.703
Gonzo.

987
00:42:33.821 --> 00:42:35.967
Look what I found.

988
00:42:38.289 --> 00:42:40.758
Captioning sponsored by CBS

989
00:42:40.847 --> 00:42:43.169
and TOYOTA.

